Therefore, the negation of the proposition is:
$$
\text{If } A \cup B = A \text{ (hypothesis), then } A \cap B \neq B \text{ (negation of the conclusion.)}
\]

Thus, the negation of the proposition is:
$$
\text{There exist } A \text{ and } B \text{ such that } A \cup B = A \text{ and } A \cap B \neq B.
\]

