\]
Using the trigonometric identities $\cos (180 ^{\circ} + \alpha) = -\cos \alpha$, $\sin (\alpha + 360 ^{\circ}) = \sin \alpha$, $\sin (-\alpha - 180 ^{\circ}) = -\sin (\alpha + 180 ^{\circ}) = \boxed{--\sin \alpha} = \sin \alpha$, and $\cos (-180 ^{\circ} - \alpha) = -\cos (\alpha + 180 ^{\circ}) = \boxed{--\cos \alpha} = \cos \alpha$, we get:
